table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "27 July 2021"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/465"} "Nippon Budokan, Chiyoda, Tokyo"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/18001046"} "34 from 34 countries"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "Just like in Rio, the 81 kg category did not go well for the favourites. Only one of the four top seeded judoka, reigning world champion " [:a {:href "/athletes/141019"} "Matthias Casse"] " from Belgium, brought home a medal. One home ground, the momentum of winning gold in the lighter classes was in favour of " [:a {:href "/athletes/134778"} "Takanori Nagase"] " of Japan, the 2015 world champion and bronze medallist at the Rio Olympics. In the semi-final, he defeated Casse with a Seoi-naga (shoulder throw) for a Waza-ari (half point) as Golden Score. In the final against " [:a {:href "/athletes/134476"} "Saeid Mollaei"] ", applying an Ashi-guruma earned him the decisive Waza-ari in the Golden Score. Mollaei reached the final collecting his second Waza-aris 2:55 min into the fight against " [:a {:href "/athletes/140892"} "Shamil Borchashvili"] ". Mollaei competed at the 2016 Olympics and in 2018 became the world champion representing Iran. When he refused to submit to political pressure not to fight Israeli " [:a {:href "/athletes/134574"} "Sagi Muki"] ", he defected first to Germany, and eventually to Mongolia, wearing their colours in Tokyo."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Underdog Borchashvili, born in Chechnya, came to Austria as a child and was trained by the German 2004 Olympic gold medallist " [:a {:href "/athletes/106415"} "Yvonne Bönisch"] ". Only 14th in the ranking list, he scored an upset victory against " [:a {:href "/athletes/143449"} "Dominic Ressel"] " by Ippon (full point) after 1:21 min for bronze. Casse clinched the second bronze medal toppling Georgian " [:a {:href "/athletes/143220"} "Tato Grigalashvili"] " with a Yoki-otoshi for an Ippon after 1:26 min."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/134778"} "Takanori Nagase"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/JPN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/JPN.png"}] "JPN"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/134476"} "Saeid Mollaei"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/MGL"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/MGL.png"}] "MGL"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "=3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/140892"} "Shamil Borchashvili"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/AUT"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/AUT.png"}] "AUT"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "=3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/141019"} "Matthias Casse"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/BEL"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/BEL.png"}] "BEL"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "=5"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/143449"} "Dominic Ressel"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GER"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GER.png"}] "GER"]] [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "=5"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/143220"} "Tato Grigalashvili"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/coun